### =====================================================================
### EventHub backend. Steps: 1) run database/eventhub_database.sql in MySQL Workbench
###                         2) put your MySQL password in application.properties
###                         3) run EventHubApplication, then press the green arrow on each request.
###
### Demo accounts (from the .sql file):
###   admin         id 1   layla@eventhub.demo         Admin123!
###   organizer     id 2   samir@eventhub.demo         Organizer123!
###   participants  id 3   mariam@eventhub.demo        Demo1234!
###                 id 4   khaled@eventhub.demo        Demo1234!
###                 id 5   abdelrahman@eventhub.demo   Demo1234!
### Re-run the .sql file any time to go back to a clean copy of the data.
### =====================================================================

### ---------- AUTH ----------

### Log in (same request for admin / organizer / participant - read "role" in the answer)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "samir@eventhub.demo", "password": "Organizer123!" }

### Sign up a new participant (/api/auth/signup does the same)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Sara Ahmed",
  "email": "sara@example.com",
  "phone": "01012345678",
  "dateOfBirth": "2001-03-15",
  "password": "Sara@12345",
  "confirmPassword": "Sara@12345"
}

### Is this email already used?
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/email-exists?email=sara@example.com

### One user
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/3

### Update profile
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/3/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Mariam Mohamed", "email": "mariam@eventhub.demo", "phone": "01000000003" }

### ---------- HOMEPAGE (no login) ----------

### Category dropdown
GET http://localhost:8080/api/categories

### Published events (optional filter ?categoryId=2)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events?categoryId=2

### One published event (tickets show seatsLeft)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/2

### ---------- ORGANIZER (organizer id 2) ----------

### My events
GET http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/events

### Dashboard numbers (same as the event_stats view)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/stats

### Upload a picture (choose a real file path on your computer)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/images
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="poster.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

"C:\Users\Kaled\OneDrive\Desktop\WhatsApp Image 2025-10-14 at 20.58.57_edd67c50.jpg"
--Boundary--

### Create an event (status DRAFT). capacity is not sent: it is the sum of the ticket capacities.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Photography Workshop",
  "categoryId": 2,
  "imagePath": null,
  "startDateTime": "2027-03-10T18:00:00",
  "endDateTime": "2027-03-10T21:00:00",
  "registrationDeadline": "2027-03-08T23:59:00",
  "about": "Learn the basics of photography.",
  "tickets": [
    { "name": "Student", "price": 50.00, "capacity": 40 },
    { "name": "Standard", "price": 100.00, "capacity": 20 }
  ],
  "venue": { "name": "Media Lab", "location": "Building D, floor 1", "imagePath": null },
  "facilities": ["Wi-Fi", "Projector"],
  "approvalMode": "MANUAL"
}

### Get one of my events (the new one gets id 7)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/events/7

### Update it (only DRAFT or REVISION_REQUIRED; same body as create)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/events/7
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Photography Workshop 2027",
  "categoryId": 2,
  "startDateTime": "2027-03-10T18:00:00",
  "endDateTime": "2027-03-10T21:00:00",
  "registrationDeadline": "2027-03-08T23:59:00",
  "about": "Updated description.",
  "tickets": [
    { "name": "Student", "price": 55.00, "capacity": 40 },
    { "name": "Standard", "price": 100.00, "capacity": 25 }
  ],
  "venue": { "name": "Media Lab", "location": "Building D, floor 1" },
  "facilities": ["Wi-Fi"],
  "approvalMode": "AUTOMATIC"
}

### Send it to the admin (DRAFT -> PENDING_REVIEW)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/events/7/submit

### The draft event 5 (Career Fair) can also be submitted
POST http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/events/5/submit

### Delete an event (not possible once it has registrations)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/events/7

### ---------- ADMIN (admin id 1) ----------

### Events waiting for review (event 4 AI Hackathon is waiting in the demo data)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/events?status=PENDING_REVIEW

### All events
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/events

### One event
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/events/4

### Approve + publish (the body is optional)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/events/4/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "feedback": "Looks good." }

### Reject (reason required)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/events/7/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{ "feedback": "The description is not clear." }

### Ask the organizer for changes (feedback required)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/events/7/request-revision
Content-Type: application/json

{ "feedback": "Please add the real venue address." }

### Take a published event off the homepage (it goes back to DRAFT)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/events/3/unpublish
Content-Type: application/json

{ "feedback": "Reported by a user." }

### History of decisions on one event
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/events/6/reviews

### All users
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/users

### Deactivate / activate a user
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/users/4/active
Content-Type: application/json

{ "active": false }

### Organizers
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/organizers

### Approve an existing user (they must have signed up first) as an organizer
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/organizers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sara@example.com",
  "organizationName": "Cinema Club",
  "department": "Student Activities",
  "bio": "Runs movie nights."
}

### Report numbers
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/1/reports

### ---------- PARTICIPANT (participant id 5) ----------

### Register for event 2 (AUTOMATIC: confirmed at once). items = ticket type id + quantity (1-10)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/participants/5/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": 2, "items": [ { "ticketCategoryId": 3, "quantity": 1 } ] }

### Register for a MANUAL event (event 4 after the admin approved it): status PENDING
POST http://localhost:8080/api/participants/3/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": 4, "items": [ { "ticketCategoryId": 7, "quantity": 1 } ] }

### My tickets (each has ticketCode for the QR code)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/participants/5/registrations

### Cancel a registration
POST http://localhost:8080/api/participants/5/registrations/7/cancel

### ---------- ORGANIZER: registrations and check-in (organizer id 2) ----------

### Participants of event 1 (the demo data has a pending one: registration 2)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/events/1/registrations

### Confirm a pending registration (notifies the participant with the ticket code)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/registrations/2/approve

### Reject a registration (the body and the reason are optional)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/registrations/2/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "The event is for members only." }

### Check-in at the door: scan a ticket code (registration 5 of event 2 is confirmed and not used yet)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/organizers/2/events/2/check-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ticketCode": "EH-5E6F-7A8B" }

### ---------- NOTIFICATIONS (any user id) ----------

GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/2/notifications

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/2/notifications/unread-count

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/2/notifications/read-all
